{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>For a keeping, for a sign.</b> As a remembrance that I chose Aaron for the priesthood, and they would no longer complain about the priesthood." "<b>And their complaining came to an end.</b> Like ״וּתְכַלֶּה תְּלֻנּוֹתָם״; this form is a singular feminine verbal noun, like תְּלֻנָּתָם, מרמוריש בלעז. And there is a distinction between תְּלֻנּוֹתָם and תְּלֻנָּתָם: תְּלֻנָּתָם is one complaint; תְּלֻנּוֹתָם is a noun in singular even when they are many complaints."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French murmure, 'murmuring/complaint'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:26.991278226Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}